# 2. TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use the following stack unless the repository already has an appropriate equivalent.

- Next.js with App Router
- React
- TypeScript with strict type checking
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui for accessible primitives where appropriate
- Lucide React for icons
- React Hook Form for forms
- Zod for validation
- TanStack Query for server-state management when appropriate
- Recharts for analytics
- date-fns for date formatting
- A suitable calendar component for interviews and recruitment events

Use Server Components by default.

Use Client Components only when interaction, browser APIs, client-side state, or event handlers require them.

Use reusable components and a well-organized feature-based architecture.

Do not make every page a single enormous component.

Avoid installing a large dependency for functionality that can be implemented cleanly with the existing stack.

