# 36. SECURITY AND ROLE SEPARATION

The frontend must respect the platform's permission model.

Students must not be able to access recruiter-only or administrator-only screens.

Recruiters must not be able to modify another organization's recruitment records.

Administrators should see administrative controls only when authorized.

However, the backend must enforce every permission independently.

Never treat hiding a button as a security measure.

Never store sensitive credentials in localStorage.

Do not expose private resume URLs, authentication tokens, or internal backend secrets.

Do not expose unnecessary student personal information in recruiter tables.

Only show candidate information needed for the authorized recruitment task.

Ensure that application status changes and other important mutations are handled by authorized API endpoints.

